{% doc %}
  @prompt
    Create a fully responsive, mobile-first featured products carousel for a Shopify storefront that dynamically displays products from a merchant-selected collection. The section must not display any visible heading, title, or label.
    
    The layout must scroll horizontally from left to right, supporting natural touch swipe on mobile and tablet devices, and arrow-based navigation on desktop. Use smooth snapping behavior so product cards align cleanly when scrolling. The visible product count must adapt by screen size, showing four items on desktop, three on tablet, and two on mobile. The carousel should have a equal space from both ends. Provide a customization for it like left and rigth paddings to minimize or maximize.  
    
    Each product card must display a product image with lazy loading and a subtle hover zoom effect, a single-line truncated product title, a prominently styled current price, an optional crossed-out compare price when the product is discounted, and an automatically calculated savings indicator such as “Save $X”. Include an Add to Cart button that adds the item directly to the cart without redirecting the user. If a product is unavailable, the Add to Cart control must be disabled and replaced with a clear Sold Out state.
    
    All visual elements must be fully configurable through the Shopify theme editor. Provide controls that allow the merchant to adjust card background color, primary text color, accent color, button background color, button text color, border radius, card spacing, and shadow intensity. Include toggles to enable or disable the savings indicator, Add to Cart button, and desktop navigation arrows.
    
    The section must be optimized for mobile usability, hiding scrollbars visually while preserving scroll functionality, ensuring comfortable touch targets, readable text sizes, and full-width action buttons on small screens. The design must prioritize performance, accessibility, and smooth interaction, avoiding hardcoded content and ensuring compatibility with Shopify’s cart behavior and product availability logic.
    
    The final output must be a complete, production-ready section implementation that can be inserted into a Shopify theme and fully customized through the theme editor.
    Also include: 
    Dynamic collection-based products:
    
    Merchant selects a collection from which up to 20 products display.
    
    The visible product count adapts by screen size:
    
    Desktop: configurable number of columns (default 4)
    
    Tablet: 3 columns
    
    Mobile: configurable number of columns (default 2)
    
    No visible heading/title/label in the UI.
    
    Product Card Settings (configurable in theme editor):
    
    Show/hide product title
    
    Show/hide product price
    
    Show/hide product vendor
    
    Show/hide product rating (placeholder or integrated)
    
    Show/hide badges (e.g., Sale, New)
    
    Grid Settings:
    
    Maximum number of products shown (up to 20)
    
    Number of columns on desktop and mobile (configurable)
    
    Slider Settings:
    
    Auto-rotate slider toggle (on/off)
    
    Slide interval in seconds (configurable)
    
    Navigation arrows toggle for desktop and mobile
    
    Padding Settings:
    
    Top and bottom padding configurable in pixels
    
    Color Settings:
    
    Card background color
    
    Primary text color
    
    Accent color
    
    Button background color
    
    Button text color
    
    Other styling:
    
    Card border radius configurable
    
    Card spacing configurable
    
    Shadow intensity configurable
    
    Add to Cart Button:
    
    Displayed per product if enabled
    
    Adds product directly to cart via AJAX without redirect
    
    Disabled and replaced with “Sold Out” if product unavailable
    
    Product Image:
    
    Lazy loading enabled
    
    Subtle hover zoom effect
    
    Pricing display:
    
    Shows current price prominently
    
    Shows crossed-out compare price if discounted
    
    Shows savings indicator like “Save $X” if enabled
    
    Carousel Behavior:
    
    Horizontal scroll with CSS scroll snapping
    
    Supports natural touch swipe on mobile/tablet
    
    Arrow-based navigation on desktop if enabled
    
    Scrollbars visually hidden but scroll functional
    
    Smooth scrolling animation
    
    Accessibility:
    
    Proper aria-labels, keyboard focus, and roles for screen readers
    
    Custom CSS option:
    
    Merchant can add custom CSS via theme editor textarea
    
    Performance:
    
    Minimal dependencies, optimized for fast loading and interaction
    
    Output:
    
    Complete production-ready Shopify Liquid section code with embedded CSS and JS
    
